WEBVTT

00:02.509 --> 00:04.552
KATARA: Water.

00:04.636 --> 00:06.429
Earth.

00:06.554 --> 00:08.932
Fire.

00:09.015 --> 00:11.226
Air.

00:11.351 --> 00:15.063
Long ago, the four nations
lived together in harmony.

00:15.188 --> 00:19.692
Then everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

00:19.817 --> 00:23.321
Only the Avatar, master of
all four elements, could stop them.

00:23.446 --> 00:25.406
But when the world
needed him most,

00:25.532 --> 00:27.242
he vanished.

00:27.367 --> 00:30.995
A hundred years passed, and my brother
and I discovered the new Avatar,

00:31.120 --> 00:32.830
an airbender named Aang.

00:32.914 --> 00:35.041
And although his
airbending skills are great,

00:35.124 --> 00:37.752
he has a lot to learn before
he's ready to save anyone.

00:37.835 --> 00:38.836
AANG: Oof.

00:38.920 --> 00:41.673
But I believe
Aang can save the world.

00:48.012 --> 00:50.265
MAN: Previously on Avatar...

00:50.348 --> 00:53.101
I came along because I wanted to make sure
you got through

00:53.184 --> 00:54.477
the Serpent's Pass safely.

00:54.561 --> 00:57.355
But now I need to get back
to the other Kyoshi Warriors.

00:57.480 --> 00:59.566
You stole Appa.

00:59.649 --> 01:01.401
Where is he,
what did you do to him?

01:01.484 --> 01:02.986
I traded him.

01:03.111 --> 01:05.530
He's probably in
Ba Sing Se by now.

01:05.655 --> 01:08.157
AANG: He's here, I can feel it.

01:08.283 --> 01:10.827
I am Long Feng,
head of the Dai Li.

01:10.952 --> 01:13.204
I understand you've been looking for
your bison,

01:13.288 --> 01:17.584
it would be quite a shame if you were
not able to complete your quest.

01:24.591 --> 01:26.551
APPA: ( RUMBLING )

01:30.722 --> 01:32.724
No, stop sinking!

01:32.849 --> 01:35.268
( GROWLING )

01:38.438 --> 01:39.522
( GRUNTING )

01:39.606 --> 01:41.065
Whoa!
Augh.

01:41.190 --> 01:42.191
( SCREAMING )

01:42.692 --> 01:46.237
( ROARING )

01:47.488 --> 01:49.782
Don't make me put this down!

01:53.578 --> 01:55.622
MAN: Put a muzzle on it!

01:58.833 --> 02:00.460
Augh, oof!

02:02.045 --> 02:03.504
Augh!

02:14.974 --> 02:17.185
( ROARING )

02:17.310 --> 02:19.270
MEN: ( GRUNTING )

02:31.532 --> 02:34.160
I'm sorry, Appa.

02:39.248 --> 02:41.376
APPA: ( RUMBLING )

02:54.972 --> 02:56.140
MAN: Ransack his saddle.

02:56.224 --> 02:58.476
Who knows what treasures
are stashed in there?

02:59.644 --> 03:01.020
( ROARING )

03:01.145 --> 03:03.481
He's tied up good,
he can't hurt you.

03:04.774 --> 03:06.651
( SNIFFING )

03:06.776 --> 03:07.777
( SNEEZING )

03:13.157 --> 03:16.828
What's your father gonna do when he
finds out we lost a sandsailer?

03:16.953 --> 03:18.037
Nothing.

03:18.162 --> 03:20.456
It's the one we stole
from the Hammi Tribe.

03:20.581 --> 03:21.958
Did you empty the saddle?

03:23.459 --> 03:24.836
That's it?

03:24.961 --> 03:25.962
Nothing but garbage!

03:26.587 --> 03:29.549
Ah, doesn't matter.

03:29.674 --> 03:33.261
We'll still make a profit from selling him
to those beetle-headed merchants.

03:43.396 --> 03:46.524
( RUMBLING )

03:47.775 --> 03:48.860
How's his temper?

03:48.943 --> 03:50.653
Uh, pretty good.

03:50.778 --> 03:52.530
( ROARING )

03:53.656 --> 03:55.450
( LAUGHING NERVOUSLY )
Most of the time.

03:56.033 --> 03:59.287
I bet someone will pay
a fortune for him in Ba Sing Se.

03:59.412 --> 04:02.039
All right, you've got a deal.

04:13.760 --> 04:15.762
AANG: Appa!

04:15.887 --> 04:17.221
Appa!

04:20.349 --> 04:23.019
( GRUNTING )

04:27.023 --> 04:29.066
He's your problem now!
( LAUGHING )

04:30.234 --> 04:31.611
What?

04:36.157 --> 04:38.075
MAN: Whoa!

04:38.201 --> 04:40.912
We need the shirshu spit darts!

04:41.037 --> 04:42.163
Got 'em.

04:42.246 --> 04:43.623
O.K., big fella,

04:43.748 --> 04:46.125
You're gonna take
a nice, little snoozle.

04:55.760 --> 04:58.221
( SHOUTING ) Appa!

05:00.473 --> 05:02.517
No.

05:03.601 --> 05:05.478
( SHOUTING ) No!

05:10.024 --> 05:12.860
( RUMBLING )

05:12.985 --> 05:15.112
We've gotta get rid of this one.

05:15.196 --> 05:17.114
He's too much trouble.

05:17.240 --> 05:18.783
We could sell him for parts.

05:18.908 --> 05:22.328
( RUMBLING )

05:22.411 --> 05:27.458
Oh, I understand you've had
a rather hard time, lately.

05:27.542 --> 05:29.877
That's too bad.

05:29.961 --> 05:35.383
You probably felt you had no choice
but to behave outrageously.

05:35.466 --> 05:36.717
Like a wild animal.

05:37.802 --> 05:40.263
But don't worry,
you won't anymore.

05:40.972 --> 05:43.391
Because I am going to break you.

05:46.394 --> 05:47.770
APPA: ( RUMBLING )

05:53.609 --> 05:55.778
( RUMBLING )

06:00.283 --> 06:01.951
( SQUAWKING )

06:03.160 --> 06:04.954
Hungry?

06:05.079 --> 06:07.832
Don't worry,
I'm going to feed you too.

06:08.541 --> 06:10.501
But not yet.

06:11.043 --> 06:14.630
First I'm going to show you
how you'll earn it.

06:18.217 --> 06:19.635
( SQUAWKING )

06:22.054 --> 06:23.222
( SQUAWKING )

06:39.530 --> 06:43.576
Of course, when you perform,
the hoops will be flaming.

06:43.743 --> 06:47.538
And if you are careful,
you won't get burned.

06:48.205 --> 06:50.166
( BURPING )

06:50.291 --> 06:52.752
You're about to be sorry.

06:54.962 --> 06:57.214
( ROARING )

06:57.340 --> 07:00.468
It's obvious that whoever
your previous owner was,

07:00.593 --> 07:05.765
he had no idea
how to handle you properly.

07:05.890 --> 07:07.767
( CIRCUS MUSIC PLAYING )

07:18.110 --> 07:19.987
I'm gonna go get
a bag of sizzle-crisps.

07:20.071 --> 07:22.031
Stay here and stay away
from that monster!

07:22.490 --> 07:25.660
Behave yourself
or you'll regret it.

07:27.453 --> 07:31.958
( RUMBLING )

07:40.174 --> 07:43.135
He's a difficult creature,
stubborn and willful.

07:43.219 --> 07:45.137
I need more time with him.

07:45.221 --> 07:46.514
It's too risky right now.

07:46.597 --> 07:47.974
Too risky?

07:48.057 --> 07:49.684
What're you talking about?

07:49.767 --> 07:52.353
This is the circus,
home of fear and danger!

07:52.436 --> 07:55.147
I want the wind buffalo
to perform tonight.

07:56.315 --> 07:58.943
If you don't behave yourself...

07:59.402 --> 08:00.611
You'll regret it.

08:00.736 --> 08:01.821
( ROARING )

08:10.454 --> 08:11.998
Let's go!

08:12.081 --> 08:13.082
See you later, buddy.

08:20.965 --> 08:25.094
( APPLAUSE AND CHEERING )

08:25.177 --> 08:29.223
MAN: Ladies and gentlemen,
now for something truly special.

08:30.933 --> 08:34.353
A noble beast
so magnificent and rare,

08:34.437 --> 08:38.107
it hasn't been seen
by human eyes in generations.

08:38.190 --> 08:39.483
I give you...

08:39.567 --> 08:42.403
The wind buffalo!

08:45.448 --> 08:47.992
( LAUGHTER )

08:50.161 --> 08:52.329
Up.

08:52.455 --> 08:53.622
( LAUGHTER )

08:53.748 --> 08:56.208
Up, you insolent cow!

08:57.376 --> 08:59.336
( ROARING )

08:59.462 --> 09:02.465
Run away, get away from him!

09:05.760 --> 09:07.762
AUDIENCE: Whoa,
amazing, fabulous!

09:19.106 --> 09:20.149
Augh!

09:20.232 --> 09:21.233
Ugh.

09:21.942 --> 09:27.031
( LAUGHTER )

09:28.365 --> 09:30.868
( ROARING )

09:31.494 --> 09:32.495
Go.

09:32.578 --> 09:33.579
You can do it.

09:38.375 --> 09:40.127
Get back here, you stupid beast!

09:47.259 --> 09:48.594
AUDIENCE: Oh...

10:11.200 --> 10:13.536
( GROANING )

10:30.594 --> 10:34.557
( ROARING )

10:37.226 --> 10:39.854
( SNIFFING )

10:52.283 --> 10:55.619
( BUZZING )

11:10.968 --> 11:14.054
( GROANING )

11:38.996 --> 11:43.250
( PURRING )

11:53.344 --> 11:55.512
WOMAN: Choose well.

11:55.679 --> 11:58.432
A sky bison is
a companion for life.

12:10.444 --> 12:12.947
( GRUNTING )

12:13.072 --> 12:16.242
I guess this means
we'll always be together.

12:16.367 --> 12:19.370
( LAUGHING )

12:22.331 --> 12:24.667
Always.

12:27.002 --> 12:30.089
MAN: ( SCREAMING )
It's some kind of monster!

12:31.674 --> 12:36.345
( GROWLING )

12:36.470 --> 12:38.013
( ROARING )

12:41.141 --> 12:43.394
( SCREAMING )

12:43.519 --> 12:44.853
( ROARING )

12:55.698 --> 12:57.449
( GASPING )

12:57.574 --> 13:00.536
Uncle, what are you looking at?

13:00.661 --> 13:02.121
Is there something out there?

13:02.246 --> 13:04.373
Muh, it's nothing.

13:04.498 --> 13:07.251
Go back to sleep.

13:07.376 --> 13:08.502
( SIGHING )

13:24.893 --> 13:27.021
( DISTANT SQUEALING )

13:27.146 --> 13:29.732
( ROARING )

13:36.989 --> 13:38.282
( ROARING/SQUEALING )

13:38.407 --> 13:41.618
( ROARING )

13:47.291 --> 13:49.168
( ROARING/SQUEALING )

13:56.842 --> 13:58.344
( ROARING/SQUEALING )

13:59.428 --> 14:00.596
( ROARING )

14:09.063 --> 14:10.814
( SQUEALING )

14:15.444 --> 14:17.613
( ROARING )

14:38.342 --> 14:41.470
( BIRDS CHIRPING )

14:47.976 --> 14:49.228
Must've been some fight.

14:49.353 --> 14:52.439
Wait, let me see that.

14:52.564 --> 14:54.858
No, it couldn't be.

14:59.988 --> 15:01.949
( GASPING )
Appa?

15:02.074 --> 15:03.909
Oh, no.

15:04.034 --> 15:05.035
( GROWLING )

15:11.500 --> 15:14.211
It's gonna be O.K., Appa.

15:14.336 --> 15:18.715
I have to leave, but I'm gonna
be back soon with help.

15:22.302 --> 15:23.679
No sudden movements.

15:23.887 --> 15:26.640
He's been lost for a while,
and he looks like he's hurt.

15:26.765 --> 15:29.017
He's shy around people
and scared.

15:29.143 --> 15:31.437
Stay low and stay quiet.

15:31.603 --> 15:34.356
I can't believe
you found the Avatar's bison.

15:34.481 --> 15:36.692
Didn't you just see
the Avatar a few days go?

15:36.775 --> 15:39.987
Yes, so he can't be
too far from here.

15:40.112 --> 15:43.073
It's our responsibility
to get Appa back to him safely.

15:43.198 --> 15:45.784
This could be our most important
mission yet.

15:48.245 --> 15:49.329
( GROWLING )

15:49.455 --> 15:52.207
Give him some space!

15:54.418 --> 15:58.422
Appa, it's me, Suki.

15:58.547 --> 16:01.592
I'm a friend.

16:01.717 --> 16:04.011
( RUMBLING )

16:04.136 --> 16:05.137
I want to help you.

16:05.220 --> 16:07.431
You're hurt.

16:07.556 --> 16:09.308
We can help you feel better.

16:09.433 --> 16:10.559
( RUMBLING )

16:10.684 --> 16:14.146
And we can help you find Aang.

16:31.288 --> 16:32.873
( ROARING )

16:36.335 --> 16:38.128
My, my, you're easy to find.

16:38.253 --> 16:42.508
It's really astounding my brother hasn't
captured you yet.

16:42.633 --> 16:45.469
( GROWLING )

16:51.475 --> 16:52.476
( GROWLING )

16:54.937 --> 16:56.480
What do you want with us?

16:56.605 --> 17:00.943
Who are you,
the Avatar's fan girls?

17:01.068 --> 17:03.320
Oh, I get it!

17:03.445 --> 17:04.738
Good one, Azula.

17:04.863 --> 17:07.741
If you're looking for
the Avatar, you're out of luck.

17:07.866 --> 17:10.827
AZULA: ( SIGHING )
I knew this was a waste of time.

17:10.953 --> 17:11.995
No Avatar, huh?

17:12.120 --> 17:13.580
Well, that's O.K.

17:13.705 --> 17:15.457
Any friend of the Avatar...

17:15.582 --> 17:17.501
Is an enemy of mine!

17:23.757 --> 17:25.717
Augh!
Uh, huh?

17:25.842 --> 17:28.971
You're so colorful,
it's making me nauseous.

17:34.309 --> 17:35.936
Ugh, ugh, ugh!

17:36.061 --> 17:37.604
You're not prettier than we are.

17:43.443 --> 17:44.444
( GROWLING )

17:45.153 --> 17:46.780
Afraid of fire, I see?

17:46.947 --> 17:48.657
That's good, you should be.

17:49.116 --> 17:51.994
Go, Appa!
Fly away from here!

17:58.792 --> 18:00.252
( GRUNTING )

18:00.377 --> 18:02.504
( GROWLING )

18:09.886 --> 18:11.054
Get out of here!

18:11.179 --> 18:12.764
You have to find Aang!

18:12.889 --> 18:13.890
We'll be O.K.

18:23.400 --> 18:26.361
Don't you know
fans just make flames stronger?

18:31.408 --> 18:32.409
( RUMBLING )

19:00.228 --> 19:02.397
( PURRING )

19:08.945 --> 19:14.493
( PURRING )

19:16.453 --> 19:17.871
( COUGHING )

19:25.337 --> 19:27.172
( GASPING )

19:31.968 --> 19:34.096
Hello.

19:34.221 --> 19:35.722
I am Guru Pathik.

19:35.847 --> 19:37.182
( RUMBLING CONFUSEDLY )

19:42.604 --> 19:45.816
I know I'm not
the person you expected.

19:45.941 --> 19:49.736
And I didn't expect to be licked by
a giant tongue just now.

19:49.861 --> 19:51.863
( SIGHING )
the world is full of surprises.

19:51.988 --> 19:55.283
( GROWLING )

20:01.832 --> 20:03.875
( GROWLING )

20:28.567 --> 20:29.568
Oh, dear.

20:29.860 --> 20:33.447
You've been through
so much, recently.

20:33.572 --> 20:35.115
Hurt and betrayed.

20:35.240 --> 20:37.075
So twisted-up inside.

20:41.204 --> 20:42.789
You're still full of love.

20:42.914 --> 20:46.835
( SIGHING ) but fear has moved in
where trust should be.

20:46.960 --> 20:51.923
I've been expecting you and
the young Avatar for quite a long time.

20:52.048 --> 20:56.094
I had a vision many years ago
of helping him.

20:56.219 --> 20:59.347
That's why I came to
the Eastern Air Temple.

21:04.019 --> 21:07.606
Oh, your emotions
are so turbulent.

21:07.731 --> 21:10.859
Like swirling storm clouds.

21:12.527 --> 21:16.239
Let the clouds in your mind
be gentle, peaceful ones.

21:35.592 --> 21:37.969
Someone looks very well-rested,

21:38.094 --> 21:40.639
judging by your bed head.

21:40.764 --> 21:41.765
( ROARING )

22:04.830 --> 22:07.457
I have prepared
a message for Aang.

22:07.624 --> 22:09.584
May I attach it to your horn?

22:09.709 --> 22:12.337
( RUMBLING )

22:15.382 --> 22:18.760
You and the Avatar's
energies are mixed.

22:18.885 --> 22:21.596
You have an unbreakable bond.

22:21.721 --> 22:26.601
By reading your energy,
I can sense where Aang is.

22:28.979 --> 22:32.566
Funny, what invisible strings
connect us all.

22:42.033 --> 22:45.370
I'll see you again, great beast.

22:47.831 --> 22:50.208
( RUMBLING )

22:59.676 --> 23:01.928
( RUMBLING )

23:18.111 --> 23:21.156
( PURRING )

23:25.702 --> 23:26.703
( RUMBLING )

23:33.835 --> 23:35.754
( ROARING )
